  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 0757563d).\n\n### What changed\n\nThe second half of #266. @austin62jake's PR #713 (merged) made the program sim sweep a Tap-kind tool at its thread's core (`tool_law::cutting_radius`, ISO 724 basic minor diameter, `d/2 - 0.5413 p`). As their PR noted, a tap on a tap-drill hole still did not post: the op's own verify convicted the tap's feed in and out (`move 1/2 cuts past the finish surface`) because its tangency and solid laws read the full major diameter against the hole wall.\n\n- New `operation::tap_core` (`acquit`, `core_tool`): for a Z drill cycle with a Tap-kind tool, generate re-runs the same cutting laws (`verify_bodies` + the containment solid law) with the tap cut to its core, and drops each `Gouge` that the core run does not also raise.\n- Only `Gouge` is re-read. Rapids, shank, holder and fixture verdicts keep the full diameter (a tap must never rapid into its thread band). It can only remove convictions, never add one; a pitch with no core leaves the full verdict standing.\n- Out of scope, unchanged (full diameter, over-reports only): the helical thread mill (`Thread` op), cross holes, tilted (3+2) taps.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/266-tap-core-verify.md`.\n\nCredit: the rule (`cutting_radius`), the sim half and the `tap_sim.rs` fixtures are @austin62jake's (#271 / #713); this PR builds on them. No code of theirs is re-committed here, since it is already on main.\n\n### Readings (M6 x 1 catalog tap, block with a blind square hole)\n\n| Case | Op verify before | Op verify after | Program sim |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ø5 hole (tap drill) | Gouge at moves 1, 2 (blocks post) | no blocking warning | clean |\n| Ø4.6 hole (under D1 4.917) | gouge | gouge | gouge |\n| Ø0.5 slit (no pilot) | gouge | gouge | - |\n| Ø5 hole, tap 3 mm past the floor | gouge | gouge | gouge |\n| Ø6 drill in Ø5 hole | gouge | gouge (unchanged) | - |\n\n### Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/tap_sim.rs`)\n\n- `a_tap_in_a_tap_drill_hole_carries_no_blocking_warning` - fails on main (Gouge at moves 1 and 2), passes with the fix.\n- Guards: `a_tap_in_a_hole_under_its_minor_diameter_is_still_convicted`, `a_tap_deeper_than_its_hole_is_still_convicted`, `a_tap_with_no_hole_under_it_is_still_convicted`, `a_drill_at_its_own_diameter_keeps_the_full_verdict`; austin62jake's two sim tests still pass.\n\n### How tested (Linux)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 74c5ba8b: app suites (lib + 131 suites incl. `tap_sim`, `solid_law_goldens`, `drill_prior`, `posting`, `tapping_mode`, `verify`-adjacent) ok in 639 s, ui suites (boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, feedback, machine, operations) ok in 114 s; 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `tap_sim` alone: 7 passed. The new pinning test reproduced on main as `Gouge { at: 1 }`, `Gouge { at: 2 }` before the fix.\n\nGoldens: no golden file changed (paths are untouched; only warnings are re-read). `solid_law_goldens` (tapped hole modelled at the major diameter) unaffected.\n\n### Not exercised\n\n- Through the GUI / `camcraft-cli mcp` post end to end (the post gate reads exactly these warnings plus the program sim, both pinned).\n- Thread mill, tilted frames, Windows/macOS.\n\nChangelog: A tap on a hole modelled at tap-drill size no longer carries false \"cuts past the finish surface\" warnings, so it posts (#266)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #266\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
